---
import InclusionDecal from './InclusionDecal.astro';
---
<div class="E-in" style="padding-top:70px">
  <div class="E-incl">
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center">
      <InclusionDecal size={200} />
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>You won't have to explain yourself</h2>
      <p>Some of this needs saying plainly, rather than being left for you to work out from a sticker on the door.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="7" fill="#C0551E"/></svg><span>The name and pronouns you use go on my file, in my notes, and in every letter I write about you, whatever your Medicare card says. Your legal name sits in one field for billing and nowhere else.</span></li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="7" fill="#DFA22C"/></svg><span>Gender-affirming voice work is a service I offer, not a favour I'll consider. You don't need a diagnosis, a letter, or anyone's permission to book it.</span></li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="7" fill="#6E7B45"/></svg><span>Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander families are welcome, and I'll work alongside your Aboriginal health worker or hospital liaison officer if you'd like. Interpreters are arranged at no cost to you.</span></li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="7" fill="#9DB2B2"/></svg><span>Bring whoever you want into the room. Partner, parent, support worker, or a friend who does the talking on hard days.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
